WEBVTT

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:02.059
The current agent does not automatically

00:00:02.059 --> 00:00:03.980
traverse downward to include every

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.720
derived instance when you query a

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:06.620
broad parent type.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.320
Why does that matter in a

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.299
real -world query?

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.559
Walk me through a scenario.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.420
Let's say a regional manager is

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.800
running a diagnostic on everything

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.140
in their supply chain that might

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.060
spoil. They sit down at the

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.620
chat interface and ask the agent

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.520
to analyze inventory risk for all

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.380
product. Just general products.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.180
Right. Because of this preview limitation,

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.640
the agent might only query the

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.920
base product entity and completely

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.380
fail to roll up the derived

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.780
frozen product instances into that

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.180
analysis. Oh, wow.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.100
So the manager thinks they are

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.740
looking at a comprehensive report,

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.520
but the AI just silently ignored

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.760
half a million dollars worth of

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.720
melting ice cream because the human

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.460
didn't specifically say the word frozen.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.480
Precisely. You have to specifically

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.540
name the relevant derived type in

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.059
your prompt.
